WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:01.254
- Tonight I wanna talk about something

00:00:01.254 --> 00:00:04.723
that you guys have been
texting and commenting about.

00:00:04.723 --> 00:00:05.750
I have two children

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.542
so I'd say I'm pretty
good at getting pregnant,

00:00:08.542 --> 00:00:11.821
but a lot of you out there
are trying and struggling,

00:00:11.821 --> 00:00:13.186
so I wanna talk about that tonight.

00:00:13.186 --> 00:00:15.955
Tonight's topic is the worst things about

00:00:15.955 --> 00:00:17.167
trying to get pregnant.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.885
If it was just about like having sex,

00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:22.196
we would not have an episode about this.

00:00:22.196 --> 00:00:24.860
So first, it gets way too clinical.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.855
When most people think
of conceiving a child,

00:00:27.855 --> 00:00:29.539
their thought is like oh you get married

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:31.965
and you go on a honeymoon,
and you just make one,

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:32.888
and that's not how it happens

00:00:32.888 --> 00:00:34.758
a lot of the time for a lot of couples.

00:00:34.758 --> 00:00:36.220
You want your child to be conceived

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.162
in this natural
environment of like warmth,

00:00:39.162 --> 00:00:40.679
and love, and happiness,

00:00:40.679 --> 00:00:42.588
and when you're charting ovulation,

00:00:42.588 --> 00:00:44.794
and you're like literally using a calender

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:46.725
to figure out the best day to make a baby,

00:00:46.725 --> 00:00:48.431
it takes a lot of the romance out of it

00:00:48.431 --> 00:00:49.798
which is discouraging.

00:00:49.798 --> 00:00:51.334
Especially if it does not work out

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.593
for you the first couple of months,

00:00:52.593 --> 00:00:54.898
it turns into this like
peeing on a lot of sticks,

00:00:54.898 --> 00:00:57.185
scheduling sex, monitoring your diet,

00:00:57.185 --> 00:00:58.727
monitoring your partner's diet,

00:00:58.727 --> 00:01:01.554
having to wait which is
such an annoying part of it

00:01:01.554 --> 00:01:02.512
because that's the way you know

00:01:02.512 --> 00:01:05.081
if that whole month was
a success or a waste.

00:01:05.081 --> 00:01:07.443
So while I know it can get
into this cycle of like

00:01:07.443 --> 00:01:09.936
non-romance, kind of clinical,

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.825
try to have as much fun
with it as you possibly can,

00:01:12.825 --> 00:01:15.880
and just make the most
of the situation at hand.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.146
And at least you're getting some you know?

00:01:18.146 --> 00:01:19.784
Like...

00:01:19.784 --> 00:01:22.484
You're having sex (giggles).

00:01:22.484 --> 00:01:24.516
So next, the jealousy.

00:01:24.516 --> 00:01:26.611
I have the most insane baby fever right

00:01:26.611 --> 00:01:30.246
and I mean insane because
now is not a reasonable time

00:01:30.246 --> 00:01:31.229
for me to have a child -

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:33.487
I have two beautiful children already -

00:01:33.487 --> 00:01:37.010
and it just so happens that
most of my friends are pregnant.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.339
And they're all posting
pictures of their cribs

00:01:39.339 --> 00:01:40.866
that they're setting up in their nursery

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:42.611
and their bump progress photos,

00:01:42.611 --> 00:01:45.196
and their gender reveal,
and all that shit.

00:01:45.196 --> 00:01:47.446
And I'm just like fuck you!

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:52.250
I love you but fuck you, I'm so jealous.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.457
What we all need to realize is that

00:01:55.457 --> 00:01:58.482
this person is not taking
anything away from you.

00:01:58.482 --> 00:02:00.267
It's not like their child is the child

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:01.738
that you could've had.

00:02:01.738 --> 00:02:03.343
So while the jealousy is real,

00:02:03.343 --> 00:02:06.417
don't try to steal it 'cause
I know they smell really nice,

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:08.000
and like you might be tempted

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.893
but I thought this through
and it's just not gonna work.

00:02:09.893 --> 00:02:11.350
You don't want to live
your life on the run

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.785
as good as their heads smell.

00:02:13.785 --> 00:02:16.832
Next, you become hyper aware of your body.

00:02:16.832 --> 00:02:20.098
Every little blip feels like something

00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:22.747
and you become this like
hypochondriac of sorts.

00:02:22.747 --> 00:02:23.769
So like for me,

00:02:23.769 --> 00:02:25.905
I would have like a little gas bubble

00:02:25.905 --> 00:02:28.439
and be like I think the baby's kicking.

00:02:28.439 --> 00:02:31.162
But it's like no, I don't
even know if I'm pregnant;

00:02:31.162 --> 00:02:32.774
like it's gas (chuckles).

00:02:32.774 --> 00:02:34.794
And it doesn't help
that pregnancy symptoms

00:02:34.794 --> 00:02:37.012
are the same as period symptoms

00:02:37.012 --> 00:02:38.424
because you're bloated, you're moody,

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:40.530
you know you have a
little bit of cramping.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.378
All that stuff like is
either period or baby!

00:02:43.378 --> 00:02:46.445
But there's just no way of
knowing which one it is,

00:02:46.445 --> 00:02:48.206
so you end up constantly
convincing yourself

00:02:48.206 --> 00:02:49.039
that you're pregnant.

00:02:49.039 --> 00:02:51.855
But I've had friends
tell me, "I'm pregnant.

00:02:51.855 --> 00:02:53.251
I'm absolutely pregnant.

00:02:53.251 --> 00:02:56.081
I pushed my boob a bunch
of times and it hurt."

00:02:56.081 --> 00:02:57.666
And I'm like no you just,

00:02:57.666 --> 00:02:59.314
you pushed your boob until it hurt.

00:02:59.314 --> 00:03:02.147
I feel like there's gotta be
a better solution for this.

00:03:02.147 --> 00:03:03.684
Like why don't our belly buttons

00:03:03.684 --> 00:03:05.810
just like pop out or something.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.530
Like what is a, it's like
a turkey thermometer,

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:09.681
like pregnant!

00:03:09.681 --> 00:03:12.061
Oh my switch flipped, there we go.

00:03:12.061 --> 00:03:14.045
So next, April Fools.

00:03:14.045 --> 00:03:16.658
I don't know who started this trend of

00:03:16.658 --> 00:03:18.725
just an announcement, we're expecting,

00:03:18.725 --> 00:03:21.526
and it's like a piece
of food on an ultrasound

00:03:21.526 --> 00:03:22.592
that's not funny!

00:03:22.592 --> 00:03:24.528
First of all, it's so overdone,

00:03:24.528 --> 00:03:27.241
it's so stupid, and it's very insensitive,

00:03:27.241 --> 00:03:29.154
and it really bums people out

00:03:29.154 --> 00:03:31.768
who are trying to conceive
and are unable to.

00:03:31.768 --> 00:03:33.122
So if you're thinking about doing

00:03:33.122 --> 00:03:35.061
a pregnancy announcement on April Fool's,

00:03:35.061 --> 00:03:36.042
it's been done.

00:03:36.042 --> 00:03:37.609
There are way better ideas.

00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:38.886
You come see me later.

00:03:38.886 --> 00:03:43.615
I will give you like 10
gold April Fool's jokes.

00:03:43.615 --> 00:03:45.638
That's all you need to know.

00:03:45.638 --> 00:03:48.171
And last, unsolicited advice.

00:03:48.171 --> 00:03:49.907
I don't know what it is about people

00:03:49.907 --> 00:03:51.933
who encounter someone who's trying

00:03:51.933 --> 00:03:54.748
and they decide to just blurt
out all this stupid shit.

00:03:54.748 --> 00:03:56.534
But I've heard the weirdest stuff

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:58.556
when it comes to trying to conceive like,

00:03:58.556 --> 00:04:00.533
oh you gotta do it everyday.

00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:01.573
Oh just do it everyday?

00:04:01.573 --> 00:04:04.364
Okay that's fine if you're
trying for like two weeks,

00:04:04.364 --> 00:04:05.921
but have you tried doing it everyday

00:04:05.921 --> 00:04:07.349
for a fucking year?

00:04:07.349 --> 00:04:09.166
Do you know how sore you would be?

00:04:09.166 --> 00:04:11.169
(laughs)

00:04:11.169 --> 00:04:12.858
Like that's just not possible.

00:04:12.858 --> 00:04:14.228
The best piece of advice is

00:04:14.228 --> 00:04:17.104
when you stop trying is
when it's gonna happen.

00:04:17.104 --> 00:04:19.240
Like what do you mean by stop trying?

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:21.050
You mean when you stop having sex?

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:25.591
I don't know if you didn't take
human development in school,

00:04:25.591 --> 00:04:27.773
but you can't just stop having sex

00:04:27.773 --> 00:04:29.409
and then magically get pregnant.

00:04:29.409 --> 00:04:30.642
It's not how it works.

00:04:30.642 --> 00:04:32.383
And I'm realizing that
I'm a total hypocrite

00:04:32.383 --> 00:04:34.525
like making a whole video giving advice.

00:04:34.525 --> 00:04:35.646
I'm just trying to help you through it

00:04:35.646 --> 00:04:36.967
as a person who's been through it.

00:04:36.967 --> 00:04:39.796
I'm just trying to create
a safe space for it.

00:04:39.796 --> 00:04:41.398
When you look into your child's eyes

00:04:41.398 --> 00:04:44.115
you're not going to remember
like the sticks you peed on,

00:04:44.115 --> 00:04:46.100
or the blood tests you took,

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.473
or the doctor's visits you had to do,

00:04:48.473 --> 00:04:50.326
and like whatever process it took.

00:04:50.326 --> 00:04:54.159
Whether it was conceiving
or IVF, or adoption,

00:04:55.229 --> 00:04:56.684
none of that matters.

00:04:56.684 --> 00:04:58.045
And however it happens,

00:04:58.045 --> 00:05:00.717
I hope it does happen
for you and when it does,

00:05:00.717 --> 00:05:02.018
it's going to be everything.

00:05:02.018 --> 00:05:04.413
So to all of you out there who are trying,

00:05:04.413 --> 00:05:07.107
may your conception be fruitful

00:05:07.107 --> 00:05:09.190
like this wine of grapes.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.379
So that's all I've got for today.

00:05:11.379 --> 00:05:13.350
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.539
and if there's a topic you want me

00:05:14.539 --> 00:05:16.148
to talk about in a future episode,

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:18.896
or any experience you have
with trying to conceive,

00:05:18.896 --> 00:05:20.211
leave it in the comments

00:05:20.211 --> 00:05:21.496
or you can always text me.

00:05:21.496 --> 00:05:24.451
I don't always respond but
I read every single one.

00:05:24.451 --> 00:05:26.378
I'd love to hear what you
guys want me to talk about

00:05:26.378 --> 00:05:28.460
and I love hearing your personal stories.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.778
And in the mean time,
I'm gonna go on Facebook

00:05:30.778 --> 00:05:32.235
and look at all my friend's pictures

00:05:32.235 --> 00:05:34.905
of their newborns to feel my baby fever.

00:05:34.905 --> 00:05:36.155
Till next time.

00:05:37.852 --> 00:05:41.814
(whines) They're so cute.

00:05:41.814 --> 00:05:44.147
Oh my god they're so little.

00:05:46.253 --> 00:05:47.420
It's not fair.

00:05:50.312 --> 00:05:51.145
*sighs*

00:05:52.091 --> 00:05:52.924
Oh my god.

